<article aria-label="Extension pg_stat_statements is not preloaded">
  <header>pg_stat_statements is not loaded</header>
  <p>
    The extension is installed on <strong><%= database.name %></strong>, but the module was not
    loaded when the server started, so it collects no statistics and its views cannot be queried.
  </p>
  <p>Add it to <code>postgresql.conf</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>shared_preload_libraries = 'pg_stat_statements'</code></pre>
  <p>Or set it without editing the file by hand:</p>
  <pre><code>ALTER SYSTEM SET shared_preload_libraries = 'pg_stat_statements';</code></pre>
  <footer>
    <small>
      A server restart is required — this setting cannot be reloaded.
      Currently loaded: <code><%= pg_stat_statements.shared_preload_libraries.presence || "(none)" %></code>
    </small>
  </footer>
</article>
